It is night in Mexico now.
"It is late now," mother says.
"It is time to sleep," father says.
I look at my family.
"Brother Diego, good night," I say.
Brother Diego waves his hand.
"Sofia, good night," I say.
She is also getting sleepy.
"A kiss for Lola," I say.
"Good night Maya," mother and father say.
There is a nice smile on everyone's face.
I wave my hand to them happily.
I end the call.
I slowly close my laptop.
Now there is a big silence in my room.
I feel a little sadness.
I remember my family.
